/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.1ScOrVAJMwJziQ3d-CW0NQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:32084577"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1661583284537,"createdAt":1661576844968,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1661583284537,"text":"I received an ARC from Netgalley in return for a review. Vacation Crush is the fifth book of the Texas Cattleman’s Club Series featuring the Lattimore and Grandin families. Entrepreneur Natalie Hastings is mortified when she realizes she expresses her feelings for Jonathan Lattimore in front of the whole town at the Texas Cattleman’s Club event. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eJonathan saved Natalie from bullies when she was 13. Her crush never subsided and has blossomed to full blown feelings. Jonathan is a rugged man who has worked on his family’s ranch for years. From the Stetson hat to cowboy boots, he is a sexy cowboy from head to toe. When Natalie was finally ready to “shoot her shot” in college, she discovered Jonathan a married man, then divorced. Unbeknownst to Natalie, Jonathan’s feelings are the same and he avoids like the plague. Interestingly, he finds her full figure sexy, while she doesn’t like that about herself. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhile coincidentally vacationing at the same spot, Natalie and Jonathan throw caution to the wind and explore their physical attraction. Ms. St. John captures the strong chemistry between them. It’s explosive and each love scene is steamy. Vacation Crush includes the elements of a fun, summer read: Sexy hero and heroine, plenty of heat, a little drama and a satisfying ending. I highly recommend it.","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1ORMHOTXWVNLJ\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.mXWb5Nql_0UsY0Ip\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:4609870":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":4609870,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/user